# The signing key release.sh needs, and nothing else. Copy to release.env, which
# is untracked:
#
#   cp release.env.sample release.env && $EDITOR release.env
#
# Every toolchain each target needs lives in that target's build container, so
# there are no paths here to get wrong. Windows, Android and the AppImage need
# only docker; the Flatpak needs flatpak-builder.

# Android ties an app's identity to its signing certificate, so this must be the
# same keystore for every version ever published - back it up somewhere it
# cannot be lost. Create one with:
#
#   keytool -genkeypair -v -keystore $HOME/keys/quackchat.jks -alias quackchat \
#       -keyalg RSA -keysize 4096 -validity 10000
#
# Without it, release.sh refuses to build an Android release; --allow-debug-key
# builds a debug-signed apk for testing, which must never be published.
#QUACK_ANDROID_KEYSTORE=$HOME/keys/quackchat.jks
#QUACK_ANDROID_KEY_ALIAS=quackchat

# Left unset on purpose: apksigner prompts for it, keeping the password out of
# this file and out of the process table. Set it only for an unattended build.
#QUACK_ANDROID_KEYSTORE_PASS=
